                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "perfect_vs_past",
                    "title": "Present perfect vs past simple",
                    "explanation": "El present perfect conecta el pasado con el presente: experiencias sin fecha, periodos que siguen abiertos y resultados que importan ahora:\n- «Have you ever managed a team?»\n- «I've worked here for six months.»\n\nEl past simple habla de un momento o periodo terminado:\n- «In Madrid I managed three designers. I left in August.»\n\nLas preguntas con «When…?» siempre van en past simple:\n- «When did you finish that job?»\n\nEn una entrevista es normal empezar con present perfect y pasar al past simple para los detalles:\n- «Have you ever…?» → «Yes, I did it in 2022…»",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Present perfect",
                        "Past simple"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Tiempo no terminado o sin especificar",
                          "Tiempo terminado"
                        ],
                        [
                          "I've worked here for six months.",
                          "I worked in Madrid for three years."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Have you ever managed a team?",
                          "When did you finish that job?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "ever, never, already, yet, for, since, this year",
                          "yesterday, last year, in 2019, two years ago, when…"
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "You've worked here for six months now.",
                      "In Madrid I managed three junior designers for a year.",
                      "I left in August, just before I moved to Bristol.",
                      "I've always enjoyed a challenge."
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "linkers",
                    "title": "Linkers: however, therefore, on the other hand, although",
                    "explanation": "Para conectar ideas en una entrevista, un correo o una redacción.\n\nContraste. «However» (sin embargo) va al principio de una frase nueva y con coma; «although» (aunque) une dos ideas en la misma frase; «on the other hand» (por otro lado) presenta el otro punto de vista:\n- «The deadline was short. However, we finished on time.»\n- «Although the deadline was short, we finished on time.»\n\nCausa y consecuencia: «because» / «because of» (porque / por), «so» (así que), «therefore» y «as a result» (por lo tanto, como resultado; más formales):\n- «We had a short deadline. Therefore, I worked late every night.»\n\nOjo: «because» va con una frase («because it was late») y «because of», con un nombre («because of the deadline»).",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Idea",
                        "Conector",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Contraste",
                          "however",
                          "The job is hard. However, I enjoy it."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Contraste",
                          "although",
                          "Although I was nervous, the interview went well."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Otro punto de vista",
                          "on the other hand",
                          "It pays well. On the other hand, the hours are long."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Causa",
                          "because of",
                          "We worked late because of the deadline."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Consecuencia",
                          "therefore / as a result",
                          "The client was happy. Therefore, they called us again."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "The deadline was very short. However, we finished the website on time.",
                      "Although I didn't know anyone, I soon felt at home.",
                      "The job is more responsible. On the other hand, it's more interesting.",
                      "Lucía managed a team in Madrid. Therefore, she has some experience."
                    ]
                  }
                },
